---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /labs/motion/
title: Motion lab
robots: noindex
labs: true
labOnly: motion
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
extraCss: ["/labs/labs.css"]
extraJs: ["/js/wallpaper-tile.js", "/labs/style-lab.js"]
---
{%- import "partials/macros.njk" as ui -%}
  <main id="main" class="lab">
{% include "partials/lab-panel.njk" %}
    <div class="lab-preview">
      <div class="wrap lab-intro lab-pad">
        <h1 class="lab-title">Motion lab</h1>
        <p class="t-small">How the JRS mark on the photo tags moves: once as the page opens, and when someone hovers over a tag. Change the settings on the left, then press Replay to see the page-load motion again. Hover a tag to see the hover motion. People who have turned on "reduce motion" on their device see the tags without movement.</p>
        <div class="btn-row"><button class="btn" type="button" id="motion-replay">Replay</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="lab-gap" data-ctl="motion tags">
{{ ui.stage(pages.shop) }}
      </div>
      <div class="lab-gap" data-ctl="motion tags">
{{ ui.stage(pages.art) }}
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <script>
    /* Replay: swapping each photo header for a fresh copy restarts the page-load motion. */
    document.getElementById('motion-replay').addEventListener('click', () => {
      document.querySelectorAll('.lab-preview .stage').forEach(s => s.replaceWith(s.cloneNode(true)));
    });
  </script>
